From: Kitsune <km2077@foxmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: promote bridged flows on HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED

The HG5382A CPU-reason histogram after a controlled 300-frame
lan3(DSA) -> lan1(GDM) bridged test is 0x0f +223, 0x0e +90, 0x0d +25 and
zero for every other reason. 0x0f is the PPE telling the CPU that it has
learned the L2B key of the flow, the flow reached the bind rate and the
CPU should bind it. The RX dispatch still sent it to
airoha_ppe_check_skb(), the sub-flow path that only commits flows which
already have an l2_flows entry, so the bridge flow was never promoted and
fdb_promoted stayed 0.

Choose the handler before calling either one. For 0x0f, use
airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_slowpath() when the frame is a bridged unicast
candidate: the ingress is a bridge port (or a DSA conduit), the
destination is not multicast, the NPU is attached, the bridge FDB maps
the destination MAC/VID to a valid airoha GDM egress different from the
ingress, and the egress action needs no VLAN rewrite. Everything else
keeps the existing airoha_ppe_check_skb() behaviour unchanged. Exactly
one handler is called per frame, so one frame cannot be committed by
both paths.

The ownership gate is not relaxed: the slow path still checks the range,
the BIND state, the native/software layout and the hardware-learned key
under ppe_lock, and the RANGE/NO_ENTRY/BIND/TYPE/KEY/ACCEPTED counters
keep rejecting and counting foreign entries.

This is 940-net-airoha-route-rate-reached-to-bridge-slowpath.patch.

Signed-off-by: Kitsune <km2077@foxmail.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
index 9970ac69b..ad8e96ad2 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1089,11 +1089,20 @@ static int airoha_qdma_rx_process(struct airoha_queue *q, int budget)
 			atomic64_inc(&eth->ppe->rx_reason_count[reason]);
 		switch (reason) {
 		case AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED:
-			/* The PPE already learned the L2B key of this flow and
-			 * wants the CPU to bind it: this is the original path.
+			/* The PPE learned the L2B key of this flow and wants
+			 * the CPU to bind it. A bridged unicast whose egress is
+			 * known to the FDB is promoted by the bridge slow path;
+			 * every other flow keeps the original sub-flow path.
+			 * The candidate test performs the eligibility checks
+			 * before either path runs, and exactly one of them is
+			 * called, so a frame is never committed twice.
 			 */
-			airoha_ppe_check_skb(&eth->ppe->dev, q->skb, hash,
-					     false);
+			if (airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_is_candidate(eth, q->skb))
+				airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_slowpath(eth, q->skb,
+							      hash, reason);
+			else
+				airoha_ppe_check_skb(&eth->ppe->dev, q->skb,
+						     hash, false);
 			break;
 		case AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_NO_FLOW:
 		case AIROHA_PPE_CPU_REASON_UN_HIT:
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
index f06ead82c..16fa642fa 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -1052,6 +1052,8 @@ void airoha_ppe_check_skb(struct airoha_ppe_dev *dev, struct sk_buff *skb,
 			  u16 hash, bool rx_wlan);
 void airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_slowpath(struct airoha_eth *eth,
 				   struct sk_buff *skb, u32 hash, u32 reason);
+bool airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_is_candidate(struct airoha_eth *eth,
+				       struct sk_buff *skb);
 int airoha_ppe_setup_tc_block_cb(struct airoha_ppe_dev *dev, void *type_data);
 int airoha_ppe_init(struct airoha_eth *eth);
 void airoha_ppe_deinit(struct airoha_eth *eth);
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
index c1ca74b4d..0d28b965b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1958,6 +1958,88 @@ static void airoha_ppe_l2b_dbg_log_config(struct airoha_ppe *ppe)
 	}
 }
 
+/**
+ * airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_is_candidate() - is a 0x0f frame a bridge candidate?
+ * @eth: airoha ethernet device
+ * @skb: frame handed to the CPU by the PPE
+ *
+ * HIT_UNBIND_RATE_REACHED is the only reason both paths can handle: the
+ * original airoha_ppe_check_skb() path for an already-known sub-flow and
+ * the bridge slow path for a bridged unicast flow. Decide before calling
+ * either path, so that one frame is never processed by both.
+ *
+ * A candidate must come from a bridge port (or a DSA conduit, whose user
+ * port is the actual bridge port), be a unicast destination, have the NPU
+ * attached and have a bridge FDB entry for the destination MAC/VID whose
+ * egress is a valid airoha GDM netdev, different from the ingress. Only
+ * the untagged-in/untagged-out action is accepted: a tag push, pop or
+ * keep needs the VLAN rewrite decision and stays on the original path.
+ *
+ * The check is intentionally cheap and racy: the slow path and the promote
+ * function repeat the ownership and VLAN checks under ppe_lock before any
+ * FOE write.
+ *
+ * Return: true when airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_slowpath() is the path to use.
+ */
+bool airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_is_candidate(struct airoha_eth *eth,
+				       struct sk_buff *skb)
+{
+	struct airoha_ppe *ppe = eth->ppe;
+	struct airoha_fdb_entry *fdb;
+	struct airoha_fdb_key key;
+	struct ethhdr *eh;
+	bool ret = false;
+	u16 vid = 0;
+
+	if (!ppe || !skb || !skb->dev)
+		return false;
+
+	if (!netif_is_bridge_port(skb->dev) && !netdev_uses_dsa(skb->dev))
+		return false;
+
+	eh = eth_hdr(skb);
+	if (!eh || is_multicast_ether_addr(eh->h_dest))
+		return false;
+
+	if (!rcu_access_pointer(eth->npu))
+		return false;
+
+	/* Only the stage-1 no-rewrite action is eligible. */
+	if (skb_vlan_tag_present(skb) ||
+	    skb->protocol == htons(ETH_P_8021Q) ||
+	    skb->protocol == htons(ETH_P_8021AD))
+		return false;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+#if IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_BRIDGE) && IS_REACHABLE(CONFIG_BRIDGE_VLAN_FILTERING)
+	{
+		u16 pvid;
+
+		if (!br_vlan_get_pvid_rcu(skb->dev, &pvid))
+			vid = pvid;
+	}
+#endif
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	ether_addr_copy(key.addr, eh->h_dest);
+	key.vid = vid;
+
+	spin_lock_bh(&ppe_lock);
+	fdb = rhashtable_lookup_fast(&ppe->fdb_table, &key,
+				     airoha_fdb_table_params);
+	if (fdb && fdb->egress != skb->dev) {
+		/* Refresh the cached action exactly like the promote path:
+		 * a tagged/untagged change does not re-add the FDB entry.
+		 */
+		airoha_ppe_fdb_set_egress_vlan(fdb);
+		ret = fdb->egress_member && fdb->egress_untagged &&
+		      airoha_is_valid_gdm_dev(eth, netdev_priv(fdb->egress));
+	}
+	spin_unlock_bh(&ppe_lock);
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /**
  * airoha_ppe_bridge_rx_slowpath() - promote a bridged frame the PPE punted
  * @eth: airoha ethernet device
